# Gate D4 route for Town04_Opt, reworded 2026-09-17 (spec: phase 2 gates).
#
# spawn 5 sits on a 3046 m closed loop with ZERO forks: waypoint.next() never
# returns more than one option anywhere on it (vision_pilot memory
# visionpilot-carla-junction-blocker.md, 2026-09-10, two full laps driven at
# 12 and 15 m/s). survey_ring.py reports loop_m = 0 for every spawn point
# because it rejects every junction FLAG; the loop's flagged stretches are
# driven without problems. LAP_M is the measured loop length; MIN_LAP_M is
# the distance the gate must see before a return within 8 m of the start
# counts as the lap closing. 2900 is about 95% of 3046, 146 m short, so the
# gate tolerates close to a 5% odometry shortfall before a run reads as
# "never closed".
#
# The booth script reads SPAWN_INDEX with a strict sed: keep it one bare
# integer on its own line.
SPAWN_INDEX=5
LAP_M=3046
MIN_LAP_M=2900
